# AtomTheme UI Controls

When a project links `juce_atom_theme` and uses `AtomLookAndFeel`, **do not use raw JUCE widgets** for themed controls. AtomTheme styling only applies to `atom::` component types that register with `AtomLookAndFeel`.

## Use AtomTheme types

| Need | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|-------|
| Dropdown | `atom::ComboBox` | `juce::ComboBox` |
| Slider | `atom::Slider` | `juce::Slider` |
| Label | `atom::Label` | `juce::Label` |
| Button | `atom::TextButton`, `atom::ToggleButton`, `atom::ToolButton` | `juce::TextButton` |
| Look and feel | `AtomLookAndFeel` via `setLookAndFeel(&atomLookAndFeel)` on root component | Default JUCE LAF |

## Setup checklist

1. Root component calls `setLookAndFeel(&atomLookAndFeel)` before adding children.
2. ComboBoxes: `combo.setJustificationType(juce::Justification::centredLeft);`
3. Sliders: prefer `atom::Slider{style, textBoxStyle}` and `setValueLabelPos(...)`.
4. On theme switch: call `label.refreshTheme()` for `atom::Label` instances.

## Example

```cpp
// BAD — renders with default JUCE ComboBox colours
juce::ComboBox modelBox;

// GOOD — AtomTheme drawComboBox / applyComboBoxTheme
atom::ComboBox modelBox{"modelBox"};
modelBox.setJustificationType(juce::Justification::centredLeft);
```

Reference implementations: `AtomTheme/demos/collections_app/`, `measurements/Chorus/Source/`.
